"michael kitts" <michael.kitts@canrem.com> writes:

>Hello,

>  I have a few quick questions.

>1) How do you get a Ring of Conflict to work?? I have (P)ut one on
>in several different games, and still the monsters did not attack each
>other. Is there something special that I have to do??

No, just wear it.  It should work all by itself.  Make sure you are
in a room with several monsters and they are close enough to each other
to fight.  Also, don't wear your ring of conflict in a shop if you have
your pet with you.  The shopkeeper will smite your dog or cat.

>2) What exactly is a Treasure Zoo? I know about the messages that let
>you know there is one on the level, but I have yet to find one.
>   So what are they, and how do I find them?

You will find one eventually.  There will be a room full of sleeping
monsters, each standing on a pile of gold.  If you make a noise, ie,
by kicking a door or chest, or you have the "aggrivate monster" instrinsic,
they will leave the room and chase you.  Otherwise, they'll just stand
there while you knock them off one by one.  Often, if you wake them up
before you find the room, an orc or other gold-collecting monster will
pick up the piles of gold.  d

>3) After reading an unidentified scroll I recieved the following message
>  "Your hands begin to glow red" I haven't been able to figure out this
>one yet??

This is the "confuse monster" scroll.  The next monster you hit will
become confused and will stumble around for a while.  Note that you need
to actually hit the monster for the effect.  If you miss it won't work.

